### 3.2 Providers and Configuration

| Provider | Rate Control | Quality Parameter | Codec Support | Black-box? |
|----------|-------------|-------------------|---------------|------------|
{% for p in providers | sort(attribute='name') %}| {{ p.name }} | {{ p.rate_control }} | {{ p.quality_param }} | {{ p.codec_support }} | {{ "Yes" if p.blackbox else "No" }} |
{% endfor %}

**Fairness statement:** Each provider was configured to produce the smallest possible file size at a given target quality (VMAF). For providers with quality controls, an interpolation search over each provider's quality parameter finds the setting that hits each VMAF target. For providers without quality controls, the single output represents the provider's best-effort encoding.

**Configurable providers:** For each clip, an interpolation search over each provider's quality parameter finds the setting that hits target VMAF scores ({{ vmaf_targets | join(', ') }}). This produces matched-quality data points for direct comparison.

**FFmpeg (naive) baseline:** In this benchmark "FFmpeg (naive)" is self-hosted FFmpeg with `libx265` (H.265, preset `slow`) and `libsvtav1` (AV1, preset 4), driven by an interpolation search over the single CRF quality knob. No content-aware preset tuning, no smart rate control — the same encoder settings are applied to every clip and only CRF varies between iterations. These are the same open-source encoders that the managed providers (Vidaio included) build their pipelines on; the benchmark is therefore comparing the parameter-selection and search wrappers around the encoders, not the underlying codecs.

### 3.3 Quality Measurement

- **VMAF model:** `vmaf_v0.6.1neg`.
- **VMAF computation:** full-video, frame-by-frame.
- **Bitrate:** measured via ffprobe on the output file.
- **BD-Rate:** Bjontegaard delta rate via PCHIP interpolation over the overlapping VMAF range.

**Note:** The VMAF model is dictated by Vidaio's API, which only accepts `vmaf_v0.6.1neg` for quality targeting. We standardized on it across all providers for fair comparison.

